WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.981
One beautiful day, two birds were sitting on a log.

2
00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:09.912
As they floated down the Nile River, they chatted away.

3
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:14.415
"Have you caught any delicious fish?" asked Mrs. Bluewing.

4
00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:21.540
"Well, I almost did several times!" began Mrs. Greenfeather.

5
00:00:21.541 --> 00:00:24.659
She leaned closer to Mrs. Bluewing.

6
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.513
"But you-know-who is lurking in the waters," she whispered.

7
00:00:29.514 --> 00:00:35.152
"You mean . . . you mean . . ." Mrs. Bluewing's eyes got big.

8
00:00:35.153 --> 00:00:43.616
"That's right! The prince of the swamp!" snapped the crocodile as he leaped up from under the water.

9
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:48.523
The poor birds nearly died of fright.

10
00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:53.236
All the animals were terrified of the great big crocodile.

11
00:00:53.237 --> 00:00:58.417
The crocodile ate whatever he wanted whenever he wanted!

12
00:00:58.418 --> 00:01:05.477
After finishing a big meal, the crocodile usually took a nap under the bushes.

13
00:01:05.478 --> 00:01:08.537
He was just about to doze off when . . .

14
00:01:08.538 --> 00:01:17.765
"Ouch!" The crocodile opened his eyes. Something was causing him pain.

15
00:01:17.766 --> 00:01:24.504
"Ha-ha-ha! I'm the strongest beast on earth!" laughed the crocodile.

16
00:01:24.505 --> 00:01:28.832
"Nothing can cause me pain!" he boasted.

17
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:32.839
The crocodile was about to go back to sleep when . . .

18
00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:41.351
"Ouch! Ouch!" he cried out. The crocodile rubbed his jaw.

19
00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:45.587
The ache was coming from inside his mouth.

20
00:01:45.588 --> 00:01:52.337
When he couldn't stand the pain any longer, he decided to go to the dental clinic.

21
00:01:52.338 --> 00:01:58.239
"Help! It hurts so much!" the crocodile roared.

22
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.876
No one expected to see the crocodile at the dental clinic!

23
00:02:02.877 --> 00:02:11.545
He had never been there before. The dentist was a very old bird.

24
00:02:11.546 --> 00:02:18.420
"What seems to be the problem?" he asked in a low, slow voice.

25
00:02:18.421 --> 00:02:23.340
"My teeth hurt!" moaned the crocodile.

26
00:02:23.341 --> 00:02:29.006
"Open your mouth and say, 'ahhh,'" the dentist instructed.

27
00:02:29.007 --> 00:02:36.483
The crocodile opened his mouth as wide as he could and said, "Ahhh!"

28
00:02:36.484 --> 00:02:42.247
The dentist's head disappeared into the crocodile's mouth.

29
00:02:42.248 --> 00:02:48.413
"How long have you had this pain?" he asked from inside.

30
00:02:48.414 --> 00:02:54.196
"Urhemghehmdogoeth," answered the crocodile.

31
00:02:54.197 --> 00:03:01.426
"It looks pretty bad. I have to go in deeper," the dentist said.

32
00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:06.031
"Urghemdogege," replied the crocodile.

33
00:03:06.032 --> 00:03:11.873
"Don't worry. I'll be careful," echoed the dentist.

34
00:03:11.874 --> 00:03:18.511
Suddenly there was a rumbling noise. It came from the crocodile's stomach!

35
00:03:18.512 --> 00:03:24.777
The crocodile was in so much pain that he had forgotten to have lunch!

36
00:03:24.778 --> 00:03:31.365
He felt very hungry. "Wait a minute," he thought to himself.

37
00:03:31.366 --> 00:03:39.018
"There is a bird inside my mouth! I can eat him!"

38
00:03:39.019 --> 00:03:44.758
"Almost finished!" the dentist suddenly shouted from inside.

39
00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:52.029
"How does it feel?" The dentist pulled his head out of the crocodile's mouth.

40
00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:58.768
"The pain's gone! It's gone!" the crocodile shouted with joy.

41
00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:07.875
"Unless you take care of your teeth, the pain will come back," the dentist warned him.

42
00:04:07.876 --> 00:04:13.359
"How can I take care of my teeth?" asked the crocodile.

43
00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.317
"You can't do it by yourself.

44
00:04:16.318 --> 00:04:20.570
I must clean them for you," said the dentist.

45
00:04:20.571 --> 00:04:27.981
The crocodile thought about his lunch again, but he decided not to eat the bird.

46
00:04:27.982 --> 00:04:36.839
Of course, the crocodile still eats whatever he wants, but he must go to the dentist for regular checkups.

47
00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:43.542
And he cannot eat the dentist, because if he does, who will take care of his teeth?

48
00:04:43.543 --> 00:04:48.599
The Nile crocodile is indeed the prince of the swamp.

49
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:55.349
He will devour just about anything, but there is one bird that he won't eat.

50
00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:01.909
When the crocodile sees this bird, he comes out of the water and opens his mouth.

51
00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:08.525
Then the bird goes to work and cleans all 64 of the crocodile's teeth.

52
00:05:08.526 --> 00:05:15.415
That is how this bird got its nickname—the crocodile bird!

